IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- Part I, Class 4 contributions: ss 15 to 18A (src lines 600-672). Part agent ssc1, LAYER 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering by a converter script, not the official text.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE is the text answering in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered".
-- The figures the Act states in its own words (GBP 12,570 and GBP 50,270; 6% and 2%) are constants "as the Act states it". The Act says
-- the figures are "subject to alteration under section 141 of the Administration Act" and the main percentage under section 143,
-- so the amount functions take them as inputs and the seat layer passes the constants.
-- Amounts are not rounded here: nothing in these sections says anything of pence.

§ `Part I -- Class 4 contributions, ss 15 to 18A`

§§ `s 15 Class 4 contributions recoverable under the Income Tax Acts`

-- s 15(1): Class 4 contributions are payable for a tax year in respect of all profits which (a) are immediately derived from a trade,
-- profession or vocation, (b) are profits chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005 for the corresponding
-- year of assessment, and (c) are not profits of a trade, profession or vocation carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom.
-- src:602 | (1) Class 4 contributions shall be payable for any tax year in respect of all profits which—
-- src:603 | (a) are immediately derived from the carrying on or exercise of one or more trades, professions or vocations, ...
-- src:604 | (b) are profits chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 for the year of assessment corresponding to that tax year and
-- src:605 | (c) are not profits of a trade, profession or vocation carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom.
@ref s 15(1) (src:602-605)
GIVEN `the profits are immediately derived from the carrying on or exercise of one or more trades, professions or vocations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are profits chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 for the year of assessment corresponding to the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are profits of a trade, profession or vocation carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(1) Class 4 contributions are payable for the tax year in respect of the profits` MEANS
    IF     `the profits are immediately derived from the carrying on or exercise of one or more trades, professions or vocations`
       AND `they are profits chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 for the year of assessment corresponding to the tax year`
       AND NOT `they are profits of a trade, profession or vocation carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Class 4 contributions "shall be payable ... in respect of all profits which" meet (a), (b) and (c); paragraph (c), "are not profits of a trade, profession or vocation carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom", is part of the description of the profits the grant reaches, not a "does not", "shall not" or "may not" about contributions; the subsection is silent on other profits (reading (b))

-- s 15(2): payable by the person on whom the income tax is (or would be) charged.
-- src:606 | (2) Class 4 contributions in respect of profits ... shall be payable—
-- src:607 | (a) in the same manner as any income tax which is, or would be, chargeable in respect of those profits ... (whether or not income tax in fact falls to be paid), and
-- src:608 | (b) by the person on whom the income tax is (or would be) charged,
-- src:609 | in accordance with assessments made from time to time under the Income Tax Acts.
@ref s 15(2) (src:606-609)
GIVEN `s 15(1) Class 4 contributions are payable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person on whom the income tax is, or would be, charged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(2) the person is liable to pay the Class 4 contribution` MEANS
    IF `s 15(1) Class 4 contributions are payable` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person is the person on whom the income tax is, or would be, charged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be payable ... by the person on whom the income tax is (or would be) charged"; the subsection does not say another person is not liable

-- s 15(3) and (3ZA): the figures and percentages as the Act states them.
-- src:610 | (3) The amount of a Class 4 contribution under this section for any tax year is equal to the aggregate of—
-- src:611 | (a) the main Class 4 percentage of so much of the profits ... referred to in subsection (1) above (computed in accordance with Schedule 2 to this Act) as exceeds £12,570 but does not exceed £50,270; and
@ref s 15(3)(a) (src:610-611)
`s 15(3)(a) the lower profits limit as the Act states it` MEANS 12570

-- src:610 | (3) The amount of a Class 4 contribution under this section for any tax year is equal to the aggregate of—
-- src:611 | (a) the main Class 4 percentage of so much of the profits ... referred to in subsection (1) above (computed in accordance with Schedule 2 to this Act) as exceeds £12,570 but does not exceed £50,270; and
-- src:612 | (b) the additional Class 4 percentage of so much of those profits ... as exceeds £50,270;
@ref s 15(3)(b) (src:610-612)
`s 15(3)(b) the upper profits limit as the Act states it` MEANS 50270

-- src:614 | (3ZA) For the purposes of this Act—
-- src:615 | (a) the main Class 4 percentage is 6%; and
-- src:616 | (b) the additional Class 4 percentage is 2 per cent;
-- src:617 | but the main Class 4 percentage is subject to alteration under section 143 of the Administration Act.
@ref s 15(3ZA) (src:614-617)
`s 15(3ZA)(a) the main Class 4 percentage as the Act states it` MEANS 6%

-- src:614 | (3ZA) For the purposes of this Act—
-- src:615 | (a) the main Class 4 percentage is 6%; and
-- src:616 | (b) the additional Class 4 percentage is 2 per cent;
@ref s 15(3ZA) (src:614-616)
`s 15(3ZA)(b) the additional Class 4 percentage as the Act states it` MEANS 2%

-- s 15(3): the amount is the aggregate of the main Class 4 percentage of the profits (computed in accordance with Schedule 2) above
-- the lower limit up to the upper limit, and the additional Class 4 percentage of the profits above the upper limit.
-- src:610 | (3) The amount of a Class 4 contribution under this section for any tax year is equal to the aggregate of—
-- src:611 | (a) the main Class 4 percentage of so much of the profits ... referred to in subsection (1) above (computed in accordance with Schedule 2 to this Act) as exceeds £12,570 but does not exceed £50,270; and
-- src:612 | (b) the additional Class 4 percentage of so much of those profits ... as exceeds £50,270;
-- src:613 | but the figures specified in this subsection are subject to alteration under section 141 of the Administration Act.
@ref s 15(3) (src:610-613)
GIVEN `s 15(1) Class 4 contributions are payable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      profits IS A NUMBER
      `the lower profits limit` IS A NUMBER
      `the upper profits limit` IS A NUMBER
      `the main Class 4 percentage` IS A NUMBER
      `the additional Class 4 percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 15(3) the amount of the Class 4 contribution for the tax year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 15(1) Class 4 contributions are payable`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (   `the main Class 4 percentage` TIMES max 0 ((min profits `the upper profits limit`) MINUS `the lower profits limit`)
              PLUS `the additional Class 4 percentage` TIMES max 0 (profits MINUS `the upper profits limit`))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amount is that of a Class 4 contribution "under this section"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether one is payable was not answered

-- s 15(3A): a member of a limited liability partnership.
-- src:618 | (3A) Where income tax is (or would be) charged on a member of a limited liability partnership in respect of profits ... arising from the carrying on of a trade or profession by the limited liability partnership, Class 4 contributions shall be payable by him if they would be payable were the trade or profession carried on in partnership by the members.
@ref s 15(3A) (src:618-618)
GIVEN `income tax is, or would be, charged on the member in respect of profits arising from the carrying on of a trade or profession by the limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Class 4 contributions would be payable were the trade or profession carried on in partnership by the members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(3A) Class 4 contributions are payable by the member of the limited liability partnership` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `income tax is, or would be, charged on the member in respect of profits arising from the carrying on of a trade or profession by the limited liability partnership` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where income tax is (or would be) charged on a member of a limited liability partnership"
        IF `Class 4 contributions would be payable were the trade or profession carried on in partnership by the members` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Class 4 contributions shall be payable by him if they would be payable were the trade or profession carried on in partnership by the members" (marginal reading M1(a))

-- s 15(5): the year of assessment which corresponds to a tax year is the one consisting of the same period.
-- src:620 | (5) For the purposes of this section the year of assessment which corresponds to a tax year is the year of assessment (within the meaning of the Tax Acts) which consists of the same period as that tax year.
@ref s 15(5) (src:620-620)
GIVEN `the year of assessment, within the meaning of the Tax Acts, consists of the same period as the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(5) the year of assessment corresponds to the tax year` MEANS
    IF `the year of assessment, within the meaning of the Tax Acts, consists of the same period as the tax year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the year of assessment which corresponds to a tax year is the year of assessment ... which consists of the same period as that tax year" (marginal reading M3: a defining "is" is read like "means")

§§ `s 16 Application of Income Tax Acts and destination of Class 4 contributions`

-- s 16(1) and (2): all provisions of the Income Tax Acts apply, with the necessary modifications, to Class 4 contributions, but subject to
-- any provision made by or under ss 17(3) and (4) and 18 (and their Northern Ireland counterparts) and Schedule 2.
-- src:622 | (1) All the provisions of the Income Tax Acts, including in particular—
-- src:623 | (a) provisions as to assessment, collection, repayment and recovery, and
-- src:624 | (b) the provisions of Part VA (payment of tax) and Part X (penalties) of the Taxes Management Act 1970, and
-- src:625 | (c) the provisions of Schedules 55 and 56 to the Finance Act 2009 and of Schedule 38 to the Finance Act 2012, and
-- src:626 | (d) the provisions of Part 4 (follower notices and accelerated payments) and Part 5 (promoters of tax avoidance schemes) of the Finance Act 2014, and
-- src:627 | (e) the provisions of Schedule 18 to the Finance Act 2016 (serial tax avoidance), and
-- src:628 | (f) the provisions of Schedules 24 to 26 to the Finance Act 2021 (penalties),
-- src:629 | shall, with the necessary modifications, apply in relation to Class 4 contributions under this Act and the Northern Ireland Contributions and Benefits Act as if those contributions were income tax chargeable under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 in respect of the profits of a trade, profession or vocation which is not carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom.
-- src:630 | (2) Subsection (1) above is subject to any provision made by or under—
-- src:631 | (a) sections 17(3) and (4) and 18 below;
-- src:632 | (b) sections 17(3) and (4) and 18 of the Northern Ireland Contributions and Benefits Act; and
-- src:633 | (c) Schedule 2 to this Act.
@ref s 16(1), s 16(2) (src:622-633)
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of the Income Tax Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision made by or under section 17(3) or (4) or 18 (or their Northern Ireland counterparts), or Schedule 2, displaces it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) the provision of the Income Tax Acts applies, with the necessary modifications, in relation to Class 4 contributions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the provision is a provision of the Income Tax Acts` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks of "the provisions of the Income Tax Acts"
        IF `a provision made by or under section 17(3) or (4) or 18 (or their Northern Ireland counterparts), or Schedule 2, displaces it` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subsection (1) above is subject to any provision made by or under" sections 17(3) and (4), 18 and Schedule 2
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:634 | (3) Schedule 2 to this Act has effect for the application or modification, in relation to Class 4 contributions under this Act and the Northern Ireland Contributions and Benefits Act, of certain provisions of the Income Tax Acts, and the exclusion of other provisions, and generally with respect to the contributions.
@ref s 16(3) (src:634-634)
GIVEN class IS A `Class of contribution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(3) Schedule 2 has effect in relation to the class of contribution` MEANS
    IF class EQUALS `Class 4`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Schedule 2 to this Act has effect ... in relation to Class 4 contributions"

§§ `s 18 Class 4 contributions recoverable under regulations`

-- s 18(1): the conditions on which regulations may make an earner treated as self-employed liable to a Class 4 contribution.
-- src:654 | (1) The Inland Revenue may by regulations make provision so that where—
-- src:655 | (a) an earner, in respect of any one or more employments of his, is treated by regulations under section 2(2)(b) above as being self-employed; and
-- src:656 | (b) in any tax year he has earnings from any such employment (one or more) which fall within paragraph (b)(i) of subsection (8) of section 11 above but is not liable for a higher weekly rate of Class 2 contributions by virtue of regulations under that subsection; and
-- src:657 | (c) the total of those earnings exceeds £12,570,
-- src:658 | he is to be liable, in respect of those earnings, to pay a Class 4 contribution ....
@ref s 18(1) (src:654-658)
GIVEN `the earner, in respect of one or more employments, is treated by regulations under section 2(2)(b) as being self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the tax year he has earnings from such employment which fall within section 11(8)(b)(i) but is not liable for a higher weekly rate of Class 2 contributions by virtue of regulations under that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total of those earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the figure in subsection (1)(c)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) the regulations may make the earner liable to pay a Class 4 contribution in respect of the earnings` MEANS
    IF     `the earner, in respect of one or more employments, is treated by regulations under section 2(2)(b) as being self-employed`
       AND `in the tax year he has earnings from such employment which fall within section 11(8)(b)(i) but is not liable for a higher weekly rate of Class 2 contributions by virtue of regulations under that subsection`
       AND `the total of those earnings` GREATER THAN `the figure in subsection (1)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "where" (a), (b) and (c) hold; (c) is "exceeds", so a total equal to the figure is outside it

-- s 18(1A): the amount payable by virtue of regulations under section 18, worked as in section 15(3).
-- src:659 | (1A) The amount of a Class 4 contribution payable by virtue of regulations under this section is equal to the aggregate of—
-- src:660 | (a) the main Class 4 percentage of so much of the total of the earnings referred to in subsection (1)(b) above as exceeds £12,570 but does not exceed £50,270; and
-- src:661 | (b) the additional Class 4 percentage of so much of that total as exceeds £50,270;
-- src:662 | but the figures specified in this subsection are subject to alteration under section 141 of the Administration Act.
@ref s 18(1A) (src:659-662)
GIVEN `the earner is liable under regulations made under section 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total of the earnings referred to in subsection (1)(b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the lower figure` IS A NUMBER
      `the upper figure` IS A NUMBER
      `the main Class 4 percentage` IS A NUMBER
      `the additional Class 4 percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 18(1A) the amount of the Class 4 contribution payable by virtue of regulations under section 18` MEANS
    IF `the earner is liable under regulations made under section 18`
    THEN JUST (   `the main Class 4 percentage` TIMES max 0 ((min `the total of the earnings referred to in subsection (1)(b)` `the upper figure`) MINUS `the lower figure`)
               PLUS `the additional Class 4 percentage` TIMES max 0 (`the total of the earnings referred to in subsection (1)(b)` MINUS `the upper figure`))
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amount is that of a contribution "payable by virtue of regulations under this section"

§§ `s 18A Class 4 contributions: partnerships`

-- src:671 | (2) “Firm” has the same meaning as in the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 (and includes a limited liability partnership in relation to which section 863(1) of that Act applies); and “partner” is to be read accordingly and includes a former partner.
@ref s 18A(2) (src:671-671)
GIVEN `it is a firm within the meaning of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a limited liability partnership in relation to which section 863(1) of that Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(2) the body is a firm` MEANS
    IF `it is a firm within the meaning of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005` OR `it is a limited liability partnership in relation to which section 863(1) of that Act applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“Firm” has the same meaning as in the ... Act 2005 (and includes a limited liability partnership ...)"

-- src:671 | (2) “Firm” has the same meaning as in the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 (and includes a limited liability partnership in relation to which section 863(1) of that Act applies); and “partner” is to be read accordingly and includes a former partner.
@ref s 18A(2) (src:671-671)
GIVEN `the person is a partner in a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a former partner in a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(2) the person is a partner` MEANS
    IF `the person is a partner in a firm` OR `the person is a former partner in a firm`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“partner” is to be read accordingly and includes a former partner"

-- src:672 | (3) Regulations under this section may have retrospective effect; but they may not have effect before the beginning of the tax year in which they are made.
@ref s 18A(3) (src:672-672)
GIVEN `the day from which the regulations would have effect` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the tax year in which the regulations are made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(3) regulations under section 18A may have effect from the day` MEANS
    IF `the day from which the regulations would have effect` LESS THAN `the first day of the tax year in which the regulations are made`
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they may not have effect before the beginning of the tax year in which they are made"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Regulations under this section may have retrospective effect" and no more; the grant is of RETROSPECTIVE effect and this function holds the start of the tax year of making, not the day the regulations are made, so a day inside the limit may or may not be retrospective; the flat negative speaks only of days before the start of that year
